  "graph": {
    "name": "Alert Logic: Scaling Storage and Delivery of Petabytes of Search Data",
    "link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PoYiSKUy8sE",
    "categories": "data_ingestion, interactive",
    "graph_usable": true,
    "notes": "Storage service to consumers and provide a search functionality through it.\n    System has two parts -- data ingestion and search.\n    Total data in store 25 petabytes. Each search query typically looks at 100s of terrabytes of data.\n    Search Engine -- MapReduce system based on Lambdas. Rich SQL syntax.\n    Search is a spiky workload. On certain gameday, the Lambda fleet scaled from 0 to 55k in an hour and back to 0 when demand went down (saving money).\n    Interestingly they use 'Erlang' in writing their Lambda logic.\n    The DynamoDB is not connected in the graph. It is likely connected to ECS."
